ed"/><a:tailEnd len="med" type="none" w="med"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="RNA editing of the transcript of the cytochrome oxidase subunit II gene from Trypanosoma brucei mitochondria.  Image (a) has a DNA coding strand and edited mRNA. The DNA coding strand begins with 5’, followed by three dashes, followed by 6 gray rectangles with AAA, GTA, GAG, AAC, CTG, and GTA, followed by three dashes, followed by 3’. Below this are three dashes, then beginning under the first rectangle is Lys – Val, Glu, Asn, Leu, and Val, followed by three dashes. Below this is the edited mRNA. It begins with three dashes followed by two gray rectangles with AAA, GUA, followed by 5 blue rectangles with GAU (U is pink), UGU (Us are pink), AUA (U is pink), CCU, and GGU. This is followed by three dashes. Below this is another line that begins with three dashes. Beginning under the first rectangle is Lys – Val – Asp – Cys – Ile – Pro – Gly, followed by three dashes. Image (b) has an mRNA line on top and a guide RNA on bottom. Most mRNA bonds down to the guide RNA with a blue dash line. mRNA begins with 5’, followed by three dashes. It then has A bonding down to U, A to U. A with no bond to A, G with a blue dot to U, U to A, A to U, G to C, A to U, U (pink) to A, U (pink) to A, G with a blue dot to U, U (pink) to A, A to U, C to G, C to G, U to A, G with a blue dot to U, G with no bond to A, and U with no bond to U. The mRNA ends with three dashes, then 3’. The guide RNA on the left, has a wavy green line down to 3’, and at the right end has an curved line down to 5’. " id="247" name="Google Shape;247;p35"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="1485900" y="3290887"/><a:ext cx="6096000" cy="3549650"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/>